WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.605
How do two pairs of words belong together?

2
00:00:02.605 --> 00:00:05.230
An analogy links the relationship in one pair

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.605
to the relationship in another. Look at night and day.

4
00:00:08.605 --> 00:00:11.555
They're opposites. Now compare happy and sad:

5
00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:14.965
they're opposites too. That's why these two pairs fit.

6
00:00:14.965 --> 00:00:18.090
We call words with opposite meanings antonyms.

7
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.165
The single colon means 'is to.'

8
00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:21.890
The double colon means 'as.'

9
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.340
Read it: night is to day

10
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.735
as happy is to sad. Notice the matching arrows.

11
00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:30.835
But sharing a topic isn't enough; the relationship must match.

12
00:00:30.835 --> 00:00:33.585
Here's another relationship from your module.

13
00:00:33.585 --> 00:00:35.260
A greeting is part of a letter,

14
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.085
just as a title page is part of a book.

15
00:00:38.085 --> 00:00:40.560
Both pairs go from a part to its whole.

16
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.310
That's a part-to-whole analogy. Keep that order

17
00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.585
when you read and compare the pairs.

18
00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:50.135
The module also names synonyms: words with similar meanings.

19
00:00:50.135 --> 00:00:53.560
Cause and effect connects a condition to its result.

20
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.960
Location connects something to the place where it belongs.

21
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.035
Start by saying how the first pair is connected,

22
00:01:00.035 --> 00:01:03.185
then check the second pair in the same direction.

23
00:01:03.185 --> 00:01:06.285
So an analogy isn't just a pair of words.

24
00:01:06.285 --> 00:01:10.505
It's two pairs linked by the same relationship.
